      <data key="d0">Pelvic Pain</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Pelvic pain is one of the common symptoms of ovarian cancer, often leading to further medical investigation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bloating">
      <data key="d0">Bloating</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Bloating can be a symptom of ovarian cancer, indicating potential gastrointestinal involvement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Difficulty Eating">
      <data key="d0">Difficulty Eating</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Difficulty eating is a symptom that may arise in patients with ovarian cancer, affecting their nutritional intake.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Feeling Full Quickly">
      <data key="d0">Feeling Full Quickly</data>
      <data key="d1">symptom</data>
      <data key="d2">Feeling full quickly is a symptom associated with ovarian cancer, often impacting dietary habits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Colon Cancer">
      <data key="d0">Colon Cancer</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Colon cancer is a malignancy that affects the large intestine, characterized by suspicious growths in the colon, classified according to AJCC staging.&lt;SEP&gt;Colon cancer is a type of cancer that begins in the large intestine and can spread to other areas of the body; it is staged using the AJCC TNM system.&lt;SEP&gt;Colon cancer is a type of cancer that can be investigated through procedures like colonoscopy, which can detect abnormalities and is linked to gastrointestinal health.&lt;SEP&gt;Colon cancer is another cancer indicated to have familial links to increased prostate cancer risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Colon cancer originates in the colon and is often treatable, especially when diagnosed early, with various treatment available.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1c1687a8a20b9c451956cf8bba241cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb68daec67dd8f436d82814b0e61ff21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Tumor Biomarkers">
      <data key="d0">Tumor Biomarkers</data>
      <data key="d1">category</data>
      <data key="d2">Tumor biomarkers provide information about the characteristics of a tumor and can help guide treatment decisions for ovarian cancer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cancer Antigen-125 (CA-125)">
      <data key="d0">Cancer Antigen-125 (CA-125)</data>
      <data key="d1">biomarker</data>
      <data key="d2">CA-125 is a protein that is often elevated in ovarian cancer, used as a tumor marker to monitor the disease.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inhibin">
      <data key="d0">Inhibin</data>
      <data key="d1">biomarker</data>
      <data key="d2">Inhibin is a tumor marker that can indicate specific types of ovarian cancer when present in higher-than-normal amounts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-96238b4b361e393ff452a09d1ce26154</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Beta-human Chorionic Gonadotropin (β-hCG)">
