      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Organ transplant recipients often require immunosuppressive medications, leading to a Weakened Immune System and heightened cancer risk.</data>
      <data key="d6">medical procedure, immune risk</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a9d0006f1c78fe4fa7bb74b756033104</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Organ Transplant" target="Primary CNS Lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Organ transplant recipients often take immune-suppressing medications, making them more vulnerable to developing primary CNS lymphoma.</data>
      <data key="d6">immune suppression, cancer vulnerability</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-dd58424a14d9942181ba4ca3c1ec81c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Platinum-Based Chemotherapy" target="Radiation Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Both Radiation Therapy and Platinum-Based Chemotherapy are used in conjunction to enhance treatment outcomes for CSCC patients.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment combination, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-50c5e5d6c7a62da56b73abb9a3384301</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Platinum-Based Chemotherapy" target="Metastatic Anal Cancer">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Platinum-based chemotherapy is a standard initial treatment approach for metastatic anal cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment protocol, therapy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-5349eed06f06d7c9bcb541ced69e4664</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Local CSCC" target="Squamous Cell Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
