    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">45.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy can be part of a chemoradiation regimen targeting cancer cells effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is often combined with radiation therapy in chemoradiation to enhance the treatment of cancer, particularly in advanced stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is used alongside EBRT in the chemoradiation process to treat cervical cancer effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy regimens may include drugs used in chemoradiation treatments based on the extent of cancer progression.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy serves as a critical component of chemoradiation, enhancing the effectiveness of radiation therapy for cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">combined therapy, cancer treatment&lt;SEP&gt;treatment approach, cancer therapy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment combination, cancer therapy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment method, combination therapy</data>
