    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">53.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemoradiation is a primary treatment approach for cervical cancer, enhancing treatment outcomes through the combination of chemotherapy and radiation therapy.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is a recommended treatment for most locally advanced cervical cancers, highlighting its importance in managing the disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is a recommended treatment option for locally advanced cervical cancer, indicating its significance in managing the disease.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is a standard treatment approach for locally advanced cervical cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemoradiation is frequently employed in the treatment of advanced cervical cancer, enhancing therapeutic efficacy.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy and EBRT are combined in chemoradiation to enhance treatment efficacy for cervical cancer.</data>
      <data key="d6">combined treatment, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;combined treatment, enhanced efficacy&lt;SEP&gt;treatment method, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;treatment strategy, cancer type&lt;SEP&gt;treatment strategy, disease management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-95c76786e9d6dbf06ddf5d55af0cf658&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ec4d44b145ca896ff1216caa90ce5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e247ae57c50c62bded7114986471226e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d04ad65c55d0dbbee5061cf3b24030ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9bfa651267335dd5e6ae5a24d85a072</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Chemoradiation" target="EBRT">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
