    <edge source="Renal Cell Carcinoma (RCC)" target="Metastatic Tumors">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Metastatic tumors describe the spread of renal cell carcinoma to other body parts, highlighting the aggressive nature of the disease.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer spread, disease progression</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Irinotecan" target="Kidneys">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Irinotecan's side effects may impact kidney function, making it an important consideration in cancer treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d6">side effects, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kidneys" target="Renal Tubules">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Renal tubules are essential components of how kidneys function by filtering blood and producing urine.&lt;SEP&gt;Renal tubules perform filtering functions within the kidneys, critical to overall kidney health and urine production.</data>
      <data key="d6">filtration process, organ interaction&lt;SEP&gt;organ function, filtration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kidneys" target="Gerota’s Fascia">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Gerota's fascia encapsulates the kidneys, protecting and supporting them within the abdominal cavity.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical support, anatomy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Kidneys" target="Urinary Tract">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The kidneys are a significant component of the urinary tract and play a vital role in filtering and excreting waste.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomy, organ system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ureters" target="Bladder">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Ureters transport urine from the kidneys to the bladder, forming a vital part of the urinary system.</data>
      <data key="d6">urinary transport, organ connection</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Ureters" target="Urinary Tract">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The ureters are part of the urinary tract that transports urine from the kidneys to the bladder.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomy, organ system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder" target="Urethra">
      <data key="d4">27.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The bladder stores urine until it is released via the urethra, completing the urinary excretion process.&lt;SEP&gt;The urethra exits from the bladder, through which urine is expelled from the body.&lt;SEP&gt;The urethra is the pathway for urine exiting the body from the bladder, vital for waste elimination.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical function, urinary system&lt;SEP&gt;elimination, urinary pathway&lt;SEP&gt;urinary system, excretion</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Bladder" target="Prostate">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate gland is anatomically located just below the bladder, playing a vital role in male anatomy.&lt;SEP&gt;The prostate gland is located beneath the bladder and surrounds the urethra, indicating anatomical proximity and functional connection.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical relationship, reproductive system&lt;SEP&gt;anatomy, organ systems</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-aa251c48fc1fccfe45605a384f743662&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7418fb993bb3daa95d8563909da1de</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Urethra" target="Prostate">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The prostate surrounds the urethra, influencing urine flow and sexual function.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomical relationship, sexual health</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-c6d28b36fe82792dfb86e98ef76b3b04</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Urethra" target="Urinary Tract">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The urethra is the final segment of the urinary tract, responsible for the excretion of urine from the body.</data>
      <data key="d6">anatomy, organ system</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-8aa2c7020ce6e89888e81972588726e3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Urethra" target="Radical Cystectomy">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Radical cystectomy involves removal of the bladder and may affect the urethra if nearby organs are involved.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgical procedure, anatomical impact</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-13e723cb8b0af4bcf2f1b0fd37912cb2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Gerota’s Fascia" target="Advanced Kidney Cancer">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The growth of kidney cancer into Gerota's fascia indicates a more advanced stage of the disease, which necessitates different treatment approaches.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer progression, disease stage</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-48e138ec8da954a5667dc785e919c86b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Non-clear cell RCC" target="Papillary RCC">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Papillary RCC is recognized as the most common subtype of non-clear cell RCC, highlighting its prevalence in the cancer subtype spectrum.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype relationship, cancer taxonomy</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Papillary RCC" target="Non-Clear Cell RCC">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Papillary RCC is recognized as the most common subtype of non-clear cell RCC, relevant for diagnosis and treatment planning.</data>
      <data key="d6">subtype relation, cancer classification</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Metastatic Tumors" target="Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Thyroid cancer can lead to metastatic tumors, influencing the treatment decisions based on their growth status and symptoms.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer progression, treatment consideration</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-121b68d5de585c87804c9bce3cdc71eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Sickle Cell Trait" target="Sickle Cell Disease">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Sickle cell trait can lead to the risk of developing sickle cell disease in offspring and requires monitoring during treatments for other conditions.</data>
      <data key="d6">genetic condition, health monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a08bd0a819ea613e781d07188a350438</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Support System" target="Meals">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
