      <data key="d6">medical guidance, patient care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a99a89bec88823cedf4c1f0cd1a78e81</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Support System" target="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML)">
      <data key="d4">7.0</data>
      <data key="d5">A strong support system helps patients through the emotional and practical challenges of CML treatment.</data>
      <data key="d6">emotional support, patient experience</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hematopoietic Stem Cells" target="Bone Marrow">
      <data key="d4">10.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Hematopoietic stem cells reside in the bone marrow, playing a critical role in the production of blood cells for the body.</data>
      <data key="d6">cellular function, blood health</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-a65ba958750476cc543741efe815c7c4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="T Lymphocytes" target="Cutaneous T-cell Lymphoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Cutaneous T-cell lymphoma results from the abnormal growth of T lymphocytes in the skin.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer type, immune cells</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-196a80cd0ae47fda3849b101cca91a15</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Burkitt Leukemia" target="Mature B-cell ALL">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Mature B-cell ALL is essentially similar to Burkitt leukemia, as both conditions originate from B-cell lymphoblasts, but they are treated differently.</data>
      <data key="d6">cancer similarities, treatment differences</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-53e3a9418b1d7916e3c8717a397bbb58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Platelets (PLTs)" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team assesses platelet levels to monitor a patient's clotting capability and risk of bleeding or clotting disorders.&lt;SEP&gt;The level of platelets is monitored by the care team to assess a patient's ability to prevent bleeding.</data>
      <data key="d6">bleeding risk assessment, patient monitoring&lt;SEP&gt;bleeding risk, patient management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Myeloblasts" target="Chronic Myeloid Leukemia (CML)">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Myeloblasts are the immature blood cells that proliferate abnormally in CML cases.</data>
      <data key="d6">cell type, disease characteristic</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-7606b44d6a30ad0519bc4c10785de79a</data>
    </edge>
