    </edge>
    <edge source="Differential Count" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team is involved in conducting the differential count and interpreting its results as part of patient care.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team performs a differential count to analyze the white blood cell types in a patient, essential for diagnosing infections and leukemias.</data>
      <data key="d6">health monitoring, diagnostic process&lt;SEP&gt;healthcare monitoring, patient assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Hemoglobin (Hgb)" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team monitors hemoglobin levels to determine a patient’s oxygen-carrying capacity and need for transfusion.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team monitors hemoglobin levels to evaluate a patient's oxygen transport capacity and determine transfusion needs.</data>
      <data key="d6">health assessment, transfusion needs&lt;SEP&gt;oxygen transport, patient management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Absolute Neutrophil Count (ANC)" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team checks the ANC to ensure the patient's ability to fight infections is adequate, particularly during cancer treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team checks the ANC to evaluate the patient’s immune response against infections.</data>
      <data key="d6">infection defense, health monitoring&lt;SEP&gt;infection risk, health assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Creatinine" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Creatinine levels are evaluated by the care team to assess kidney function and diagnose potential renal issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Creatinine levels help the care team determine kidney function health and any necessary interventions.</data>
      <data key="d6">kidney assessment, diagnostic testing&lt;SEP&gt;kidney health, medical assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Blood Urea Nitrogen (BUN)" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">16.0</data>
      <data key="d5">BUN levels are monitored by the care team to check kidney performance and to help diagnose renal dysfunction.&lt;SEP&gt;BUN levels indicate kidney functionality and are assessed by the care team.</data>
      <data key="d6">kidney assessment, health evaluation&lt;SEP&gt;kidney function, diagnostic indicator</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Electrolytes" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Electrolyte levels are closely observed by the care team since they affect multiple physiological functions, including hydration and heart rhythm.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team monitors electrolyte levels to ensure proper physiological function and balance.</data>
      <data key="d6">electrolyte balance, health monitoring&lt;SEP&gt;nutritional balance, health monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Liver Function Tests (LFTs)" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">18.0</data>
      <data key="d5">LFTs provide vital information to the care team about liver health and necessary interventions.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team performs liver function tests to understand the liver's health and its ability to process substances in the blood.</data>
      <data key="d6">liver health assessment, diagnostic process&lt;SEP&gt;liver health monitoring, diagnostic assessment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Vitamin B12 and Folic Acid" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">15.0</data>
      <data key="d5">The care team monitors levels of B12 and folic acid to support cell formation and overall health.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team monitors levels of Vitamin B12 and folic acid to ensure adequate blood cell formation and overall health of the patient.</data>
      <data key="d6">nutritional health, patient care&lt;SEP&gt;nutritional monitoring, patient care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-9fa573748870dc50a98a935843997c68</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Human Leukocyte Antigen (HLA)" target="Care Team">
      <data key="d4">17.0</data>
      <data key="d5">HLA typing by the care team is critical for determining donor compatibility in organ transplants and assessing rejection risk.&lt;SEP&gt;The care team performs HLA typing for matching organ transplants and assessing rejection risks.</data>
      <data key="d6">transplant compatibility, immune response&lt;SEP&gt;transplant matching, immune assessment</data>
