      <data key="d5">Radioactive Iodine Therapy is sometimes used following a Total Thyroidectomy to destroy any remaining thyroid cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgical treatment, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="RAI Therapy">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">RAI therapy is utilized post-total thyroidectomy to eradicate any remaining thyroid cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgical therapy, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Papillary Thyroid Cancer">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total thyroidectomy is recommended for aggressive cases of papillary thyroid cancer that have spread beyond the thyroid.</data>
      <data key="d6">treatment protocol, cancer management</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-e74c94f9f2ff33172671e8742338c6d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Oncocytic Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total thyroidectomy is often recommended for suspected oncocytic carcinoma that has grown beyond the thyroid, indicating an invasive nature.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgery recommendation, cancer treatment</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Follicular Thyroid Carcinoma">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Total thyroidectomy is advised for invasive follicular thyroid carcinoma cases to ensure complete removal of the malignancy.</data>
      <data key="d6">surgery recommendation, aggressive cancer</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Levothyroxine">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">After total thyroidectomy, lifelong levothyroxine therapy is often required to maintain normal thyroid hormone levels.</data>
      <data key="d6">hormone replacement, post-surgery care</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Thyroglobulin (Tg) Level">
      <data key="d4">9.0</data>
      <data key="d5">After total thyroidectomy, measuring thyroglobulin (Tg) levels is critical to assess for any remaining thyroid cancer cells.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-operative evaluation, cancer monitoring</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-b8a273f96e02707e2e87fc43353ed57f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Total Thyroidectomy" target="Monitoring and Follow-Up Care">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Monitoring and follow-up care is essential after total thyroidectomy to assess for any signs of cancer recurrence.</data>
      <data key="d6">post-surgery care</data>
