      <data key="d5">Imaging Tests are essential in confirming prostate cancer diagnoses, determining cancer stage and treatment planning, especially post-treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging tests are conducted to evaluate whether prostate cancer has spread, guiding treatment decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Imaging tests are utilized to determine the extent of prostate cancer and influence treatment decisions based on staging outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d6">assessment, cancer management&lt;SEP&gt;diagnosis, treatment planning&lt;SEP&gt;diagnostic tools, treatment planning</data>
      <data key="d7">chunk-789ec6c06f8c999ac21c89b085b3fdb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3958b5f7df8a8fc2661705e37dc1e06</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Imaging Tests" target="Cervical Cancer">
      <data key="d4">8.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Imaging tests are essential for monitoring cervical cancer after treatment to check for recurrence or metastasis.</data>
