    <edge source="Systemic Therapy" target="Chemotherapy">
      <data key="d4">72.0</data>
      <data key="d5">Chemotherapy is a form of systemic therapy designed to target cancer cells throughout the body in AML patients.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a form of systemic therapy specifically targeting fast-dividing cells across the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a form of systemic therapy that is integral in treating various cancers, including inflammatory breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a specific type of systemic therapy aimed at killing cancer cells with drugs.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy that plays a critical role in treating various cancers, including inflammatory breast cancer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemotherapy is a type of systemic therapy that uses drugs to combat cancer cells in the body.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic Therapy often includes Chemotherapy as a vital treatment option in advanced cases of Squamous Cell Carcinoma.&lt;SEP&gt;Systemic therapy includes chemotherapy, which targets cancer throughout the body, often following localized treatments.</data>
